From: Project SunUEFI
Subject: [PATCH] camera: serve native manual controls from the existing frame owner

Apply after debian-piano a75f8c5d5fa099d65c171ac839c2e3bb6c63ec45
and the CCM, startup/stable 3A and frame-integrity patches. The exact
prerequisite camera source SHA256 is:
0a96e7d4aa2dd23bd1f49cbdfae37578327f47d3a9118464cbdfd924bf9f6f1d

Use a fixed root:video UNIX seqpacket socket in the existing poll loop.
Query actual driver capabilities and values; serialize named control writes
with independent AE/AWB/AF ownership and require successful readback.
Inactive cameras and unsupported front focus are refused. No second daemon,
arbitrary node/ioctl or inferred ISO/Kelvin/focal-distance conversion.
The CLI source is maintained separately at linux/userspace/piano-camera-ctl.c.

The resulting daemon and CLI compiled and statically linked for AArch64.
Hardware control and automatic/manual switching have not been tested.
---
